WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Conquest of the Crystal Palace.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.220
You'll face the baddest, meanest enemies ever seen on the NES.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:30.480
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.480
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.320
That's it. Two people's fine.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.560
We can make do. Yeah, I'm not upset about it at all.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.160
Yeah, that's whatever.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.700
Two people can conquest a Crystal Palace.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:52.620
I mean, if you know what you're doing and you just work hard, we can do anything together.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.580
But can one person conquest a Crystal Palace?

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.840
It feels like a conquest is usually like an army thing.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:05.860
You know, like a whole country is going to go conquest other countries or something.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.460
It's not usually like something like one person does.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:20.780
I mean, it kind of depends on if you have like maybe a dog that's lived a thousand years before he became your dog.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:21.920
That'll help. Yeah.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.340
I mean, I think if you have something like that, you could conquest things.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.740
Otherwise, no.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.440
Otherwise, it's just it's just not feasible.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:36.560
And this game is a side scrolling action platformer developed by Quest.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.180
And Quest went on to make a bunch of other games.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:47.000
But most notably, a lot of their talent will go on to then make the Ogre Battle and Final Fantasy Tactics games.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.520
So a lot more strategy than action platformery.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:57.000
But what we've got here today is not just like so action platformer.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:02.700
I always think it's like an interesting term because platformer in itself is usually like, yeah, this is a game about jumping.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.840
Right. And like action games are usually like this is a game about shooting.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.340
But this is not necessarily like an adventure game.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.520
So, Sean, help me out here.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.380
What what is like what is the distinct loop of this game?

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:26.040
Yeah, I always thought that action platformer and it's all like I wouldn't say it's overgenrification, but there's very little difference.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:35.120
It actually it shares some things with something like Mario and and Zelda 2.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:43.080
And I think that there's like it's basically you go to the right and you you you don't jump on things.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:51.840
I think the actual the actual difference between platformers and action platformers is that you can't kill enemies by jumping on them.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.320
You have to seem silly.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.940
You have to shoot or you have to do some kind of melee attack.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:02:59.960
And that's the difference.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.140
Who's to say that jumping on anything wouldn't hurt it?

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.020
Well, I guess I try jumping on someone.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.460
I haven't.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.980
I don't have that kind of vertical.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:14.600
And I try not to jump on people that are lying down because I feel like they're trying to sleep.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.780
So maybe it works if they lay down first.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:28.940
And while we were talking about one person conquesting a Crystal Palace at the beginning of the episode, it's not our hero who has done the conquesting.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:30.820
It is the demon Zaras.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.960
He has taken over the Crystal Palace.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:42.820
And so Prince Farron and his guardian dog Zap have to reclaim the occupied kingdom across a variety of stages.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.260
Really like five levels.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:53.540
But it likes calling them levels is a little interesting because they're they're longer than like a Super Mario Brothers style level.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.020
So five is like selling it short.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.940
They're a bit more into it than that.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:03.760
But there are shops along the way to kind of upgrade the character ever so slightly.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:04.860
This isn't an RPG.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:15.580
But obviously, just like any good platformer, every level ends with a big boss fight that kind of is the gate that will prevent you from making progress.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.060
Let's just talk about Prince Farron for a second.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.200
I don't want to talk about Prince Farron.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.560
Oh, OK. Yeah, no, we'll talk about the controls.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.020
Yeah, that's what I was going to say.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.500
The controls of any platformer make or break the game.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.600
So he has he has a couple different sub weapons.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.320
But most notably, he has that sword and he has a jump.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:42.520
How are those two things in the grand scheme of platformers we've played on the NES?

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:44.500
They're fine.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.680
Like it's tight. There are no complaints on the jump or the attack.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.800
Like the hitboxes seem to work.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.640
The jump you can control in midair, but it's not floaty.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.840
Thankfully, we're past the point where that's sort of in question.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:08.200
Every other game, you are able to upgrade both of both of these things.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:17.720
Some with like short term, like disposable upgrades and some with more long term things.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.460
And you can get like a fireball move later.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:25.040
But the basics, they're nothing to complain about.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:42.020
And the biggest, you know, differentiator here or the standout feature of the game is that at the beginning of the game, when you start it, you kind of choose a one of three crystals for Prince Farron that change a little bit about his like stats.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.040
They are there's the life crystal, the spirit crystal and the flight crystal.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:51.180
And depending on which one you choose, it changes the game a little bit.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.880
It doesn't change the levels, doesn't change the types of enemies.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.860
It changes how Prince Farron behaves.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.200
Sean, which one did you go with?

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.780
Well, I just I read what they described.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:06.900
And first, I just we need we need to acknowledge that my one off comment earlier wasn't just me wanting to talk about a dog.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:13.120
Like you were presented these choices by your dog, who apparently knows everything.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.940
Like he's your Lord dump.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.760
Like the dog is suspicious a little bit.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.560
I'm not saying it's suspicious.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:27.720
I think like it reminded me a lot of that scene in Anchorman where like the dog sort of does a long monologue to the bears.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.500
And if you remember that movie at all, I do.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:36.100
Yeah. Okay. Yeah. And it's just the dog is very wise.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.640
He knows more about the world than you do.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.660
Like apparently you as the main character would not be on this quest unless your dog told you what was going on.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.260
But anyway, yeah, he then gives you this choice.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:58.060
And the description of it is like pretty obvious that you're going to that you should go with the like you get a ranged weapon off the bat.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:08.620
Now, I'm pretty sure that this is really only changing the first like few minutes of the game because you can then buy the other upgrades almost immediately.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.360
And that's surprising, right?

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:18.880
Yeah. I was a little disappointed that they were that that it was that that small of like just a change in initial conditions.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.460
But it's still cool, I guess, that you can do that.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.220
And yes, I wasn't expect I was expecting to alter things a little more.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:36.780
I agree with you that you read the descriptions and it, you know, obviously life gives you more HP and flight gives you a higher jump.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:43.280
I was expecting those things to matter a little more in the gameplay like, you know, oh, more height makes it easier to dodge enemies.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:50.180
So, you know, even though I'll be a little floaty or whatever, I'll be able to like get through the level faster and not have to like worry about every enemy I encounter.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.700
I can just kind of get around them.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.920
Whereas like life is like, yeah, I mastered the combat.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.040
So it doesn't matter.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.960
I'll take a little more hits, but I'll be able to fight.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.280
And then the spirit one gives you unlimited fireballs.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.020
And that just seems like the clear winner of the three, right?

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.120
Yeah, it's not even close.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.240
It's not even close.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:15.220
I mean, and there are some enemies that are not affected by them, but they are so few and far between that it's like, OK, I guess I got to switch to the sword.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:19.400
And I think like it also is just they are slow fireballs.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:26.460
So you may just want to stick with the sword for stretches of this game, but it's still like so versatile.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.960
Right. I just feel like unlimited of something is great.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.820
It'd be like if the life one gave you unlimited HP, right?

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.840
Like you would obviously pick that.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:39.560
Unlimited is such a stat changer compared to a slightly higher jump.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:44.900
Mm hmm. OK, we can now talk about Zap in the game, at least.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:56.540
The dog. You you explained to kind of his reason for being in the game, but he's also not not necessarily a playable character, but a summonable character.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:59.440
And you can summon Zap on the attack screen.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:10.900
One thing I didn't realize is that he has like like you can see his health bar and everything, but that like you could also just retract him and use him when the when the moments are right.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:15.140
Yeah. So it's not something you want to just like call and have hang out in the beginning of the stage.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:19.080
Yeah, because he does take damage pretty rant.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:23.820
Like he does just sort of flail about the screen pretty randomly and he will target enemies.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:29.740
But he also just runs into oncoming traffic like, you know, like maybe a dog would.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:36.100
But I think that I was I was sort of experimenting with the controls.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:40.180
I'm like, there's got to be a way I can take the dog back because it's just he's just draining.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.020
And I'm sure there's a boss coming up.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:53.480
So I found, you know, if you just sort of cycle through it again and select the upgrade as it would like if you were just selecting another upgrade, he does go back into the pokeball.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:10:07.040
And I tried to like save him for boss fights, but I could never tell what he was actually doing because there's no like there's no boss health meter and there isn't a lot of feedback with damage.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:13.020
So it's just sort of seeing the dog run around and jump at the enemies.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:19.800
And if you were to then buy the dog whistle upgrade, he then does that really fast.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:33.120
Yes, but I will say that I think Zap was a little more useful than you're giving him credit for, particularly if, you know, you're dealing with enemies in later stages that like suck.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:37.220
You know, there are there are there are enemies that are easily defeatable and those are great.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.360
But then sometimes there's a lot of enemies that suck in this game.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:44.600
Yeah, exactly. Just a bit more tedious or things that like will hit you.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.840
And, you know, you just get like I'm thinking about I think it's even on the second, maybe second or third stage.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:54.000
There's like these hands that just are like attached to the floor.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:58.860
And they're not like I don't even know what you can do with them or if you can even fight back on them.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.380
You can you can kill them.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.920
But it's better to handle that.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.400
Yeah, that's true. That's true.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:09.080
Does he grab Zap's I never really deployed Zap against them.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:17.960
Well, see, the problem is with Zap's attack animation, you wouldn't it wouldn't be communicated to you if he's being grabbed because he's he sticks with the enemy that he's attacking anyway.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.740
Ah, yes. Yeah.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.200
You know, so it doesn't it's not really I would say overall.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.680
While while the combat in this game is just fine, it's serviceable.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:33.900
The the like animation of the combat in general leaves a lot to be desired.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:42.680
It has that issue with the sword where like you can't quite tell if like the edge of your sword is actually connecting with the enemies.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:46.360
It's not it's not a terrible hit hit box or whatever.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:54.020
It's just one of those things where it's like, well, you know, like what is the hit box the entirety of the sword or is like is my swing like just barely missing?

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.220
I hate that in games.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.080
That happens a lot on not just any.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.040
It's also just like audio feedback isn't quite there.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:01.400
Yeah, exactly.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:06.820
So I think like overall, it leads a little bit more to be desired in that in that category.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:14.140
The next thing I wanted to talk about the I guess you could call it an economy, but really it's about the shops.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.300
There are mid mid stage shopkeepers.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:24.700
I think it's the same girl every time named Kim and she'll sell you food items and weapons.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.580
And she's the shopkeeper so you can buy these things from her.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:34.380
But she's also the like QNN, which is presumably a play on CNN.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.940
Maybe they have something in Japan that has an NN as well.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.000
She's the news reporter there.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:46.680
And that's like that's the cutest part of the game is her giving like this little like I don't know.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:51.260
It's like it's like meta, but it's also like, you know, because there's no reason for them to have TVs.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:55.060
Right. Like, so this is who's this broadcast directly to the player.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:13:01.000
And we weren't given that in the lore dump, like what kind of what kind of media landscape they're in.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:07.260
But I guess we do have a news network that spans all the planes of existence.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:17.780
The one thing that I thought was funny about that whole like concept is you you have to sort of linger in the shop for it to happen.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:22.000
Yes. It's just like you it's not after you buy anything.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:24.120
It's not as soon as you jump in.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:27.940
It's like you could be mid scroll, like just trying to get to something to buy.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.280
And it'll be like, do you want to listen to the news?

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.220
And like, of course, you want to listen to the news.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:38.230
And there's some like like not I wouldn't say they're like little hints sometimes.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.540
Otherwise, it's just funny stuff.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:14:14.840
Yeah. Thank you.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:50.960
Knowing that Zap and the Shop are optional things within the game that obviously greatly help the player,

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:57.160
you think there's any merit for a no Zap or a no Shop challenge run?

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.940
Is that worth recommending, or is that just making it boring?

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:02.940
Have we ever recommended anything like that?

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.620
No, never. I'm just saying...

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:06.340
I'm sure they exist.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.260
Yeah, but you know what I mean, right?

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:11.780
It's like Super Mario Bros., you can't recommend a no-jump run.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:18.100
Yeah, but it's like, you could do the Warpless, so if you're doing speedruns...

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:23.560
I'm sure there's speedrun categories for no Shop or anything like that.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:27.280
There is all levels. In Super Mario Bros., there's all levels.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.200
Yeah. Okay.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.560
Does the game communicate the danger of the enemies well?

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.060
And I don't mean how strong they are.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:43.880
I mean, like, sometimes in platformers, enemies just appear as soon as the screen scrolls and it's very fast.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:50.800
Do you have a fair shot against the spawning of enemies in this action platformer?

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:51.940
Sometimes.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:16:05.400
I think that the spawn behavior, like, in the middle of a level, like when you're just sort of moving around, is fine.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.920
And there's actually long stretches where you don't see anything.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:15.020
But then there are some, I guess, like, planned fights or like more...

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:16.920
I wouldn't call them...

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.720
I guess there's one that is a boss, but it's just a bunch of spiders.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.220
And that is just the...

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:25.160
That was the worst boss.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:30.300
Because it's literally just a bunch of spiders that kind of pop out of nowhere.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:35.500
There's no, like, telegraphing of where they're going to come from.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:37.460
They're just going to come all over the place.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.840
Come from all over the place.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.380
And you're just going to keep getting hit.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:46.000
And I think that that was part of...

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:54.080
I got annoyed when you were earlier describing just some of the frustrations.

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.760
That was definitely one of them.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:01.660
Yeah, I would agree that on the most part, the game doesn't have any, like, cheap spawns or anything.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:05.040
There are just tough enemies in the game.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.860
There are just tough setups with, like, anything...

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:13.320
Anytime you're running into falling water or lava, it is probably the most tedious shit in the game.

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:17.120
Yeah, even from the very first level, the water is there.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:21.480
But, like, I feel like the...

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.000
Because those aren't enemies, right?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.000
So you can't even hurt them.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:28.740
But, like, yeah, some of the more, like, challenging platforming of the game.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.960
It's like, it's never about, like, pitfalls or anything.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.540
Or, like, oh, there's going to be a tricky jump.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:36.460
It's usually about, like, well, there's an enemy on this thing.

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:37.920
And I've got to get there.

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.560
And, you know, so on and so forth.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.380
It's like, it requires a little bit more thinking.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.860
Good players will know what to do.

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:48.200
It's not so challenging that it's an auto-death or something like that.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.540
But then the other thing, which I noticed right away in the first level,

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:59.980
the first boss is nowhere near on the same difficulty scale as the level itself was.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:01.160
Do you agree with me?

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.320
Or was I just really bad at this boss fight?

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:08.900
This is the one with the guy on the ground and, like, the lightning bird above.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.260
Yeah, which is a really cool combo.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:18.660
Don't get me wrong. I thought that was a very interesting boss because the guy on the ground is sending the electricity to the flying creature.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.780
So that then, like, charges it up to throw a lightning bolt at you.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:23.740
Yeah. So it's very involved.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:26.700
I liked thinking about dodging it and everything.

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:29.920
I just feel like attacking both of those enemies was actually pretty tricky.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.500
So, excuse me.

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:35.960
Here's what I did at first.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:39.140
I just had Zap take care of the guy on the ground.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.600
